    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d647">

                <pb facs="0903" n="777" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg777"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.00/80</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary to the President</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sanders</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lynn, Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-07-10"><hi rendition="#italic">July 10,
                        1925.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 14.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Grew</hi>: This will acknowledge your
                    favor of the 7th addressed to the President,<anchor n="82" xml:id="d647-f1"/> in
                    which you enclosed a copy of a note received by the Department from the British
                    Chargé d’Affaires<anchor n="83" xml:id="d647-f2"/> setting forth the comments of
                    the British Government on the issues <pb facs="0904" n="778" xml:id="pg778"/>
                    raised by the Chinese Government’s identic notes to the Legations in Peking of
                    June 24th, and also your letter of July 8th<anchor n="84" xml:id="d647-f3"/> in
                    which you enclosed two additional notes received from the British Chargé
                    d’Affaires on the same subject, dated, respectively, July 6th and 7th.<anchor
                        n="85" xml:id="d647-f4"/> The President has directed me to advise you that
                    he thinks in the circumstances the Secretary of State should use his judgment
                    but cooperate as far as possible with the other interested powers, using great
                    care not to have China think there is a division of counsel.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Everett Sanders</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
